<!doctype html>
<html
  {% if request.design_mode %}
    class="shopify-design-mode"
  {% endif %}
  lang="en-GB"
>
  <head>
    {%- comment -%}
      Favicon: bundled longeva-favicon-{16,32}.png + .ico is the canonical
      brand mark (Varsha 2026-05-07: admin-uploaded favicon was a tiny
      dot, the bundled version is the bold ivory L on brand-dark). The
      bundled assets win regardless of settings.favicon to keep the
      brand mark consistent across deploys. To replace, swap the PNG
      files in /assets via theme editor or git push, do not rely on
      Theme Settings > Logo and favicon > Favicon.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="32x32" href="{{ 'longeva-favicon-32.png' | asset_url }}">
    <link rel="icon" type="image/png" sizes="16x16" href="{{ 'longeva-favicon-16.png' | asset_url }}">
    <link rel="shortcut icon" type="image/x-icon" href="{{ 'longeva-favicon.ico' | asset_url }}">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="{{ 'longeva-apple-touch.png' | asset_url }}">
    <link rel="mask-icon" href="{{ 'longeva-safari-pinned.svg' | asset_url }}" color="#2D190E">
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#2D190E">
    <meta name="msapplication-TileColor" content="#2D190E">

    {%- comment -%}
      Resource hints (added 2026-05-12).
      preconnect: warm the connection (DNS + TCP + TLS) before the page
      needs the origin. dns-prefetch is cheaper but only resolves DNS.

      - cdn.shopify.com: served by every asset_url. crossorigin required
        because we fetch fonts (anonymous) from this origin.
      - api.sesami.co: Sesami calendar slots and reservation fetches.
        Fires on every service page; cold RTT previously cost ~100-200ms
        on first-paint to first-slot-render.
      - monorail-edge.shopifysvc.com: Shopify analytics beacon. Lower
        priority; dns-prefetch is enough.

      Klaviyo/GA4/Meta Pixel preconnects intentionally absent: not
      currently wired up (Klaviyo on hold per Anthony 2026-04-20). Add
      here if/when those apps go live.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- # theme-check-disable RemoteAsset -%}
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://cdn.shopify.com" crossorigin>
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://api.sesami.co" crossorigin>
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://monorail-edge.shopifysvc.com">
    {%- # theme-check-enable RemoteAsset -%}

    {% comment %} This a way to wait for main content to load when navigating to a new page so that the view transitions can work consistently {% endcomment %}
    {% if settings.transition_to_main_product or settings.page_transition_enabled %}
      <link
        rel="expect"
        href="#MainContent"
        blocking="render"
        id="view-transition-render-blocker"
      >
    {% endif %}

    {%- render 'meta-tags' -%}
    {%- render 'stylesheets' -%}
    {%- render 'fonts' -%}
    {%- render 'scripts' -%}
    {%- render 'theme-styles-variables' -%}
    {%- render 'color-schemes' -%}

    {%- comment -%}
      Longeva brand assets, loaded once per page.
      Poppins (body font) is now self-hosted. Eliminates the
      fonts.googleapis.com -> fonts.gstatic.com cross-origin chain
      and the print-media swap dance. The 400-latin weight is
      preloaded for first paint; 500/600 fetched lazily by the
      browser as encountered. Latin-ext subsets fetched only when
      the document contains characters in that range, courtesy of
      unicode-range matching.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- render 'longeva-fonts' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      preload: true on longeva-pages.css so the brand stylesheet is
      discovered alongside meta-tags / fonts / theme-variables in the
      head, not after the rest of the head finishes parsing. Same
      pattern Horizon uses for base.css.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {{ 'longeva-pages.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag: preload: true }}
    <script src="{{ 'longeva-animations.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>

    {%- comment -%}
      Sesami widget script tag REMOVED 2026-05-08. Verified
      `experience.sesami.co` is NXDOMAIN (Sesami deprecated the
      standalone CDN subdomain). The Shopify app embed for Sesami
      now injects everything needed: sesami-main.js, the
      <sesami-experience> custom element registration, and the
      variant form data scaffolding. Admin must toggle the Sesami
      app embed ON in Customise > App embeds for the booking flow
      to work end-to-end. Without the app embed, the
      <sesami-experience> elements still render the slot preview
      (via sesami-main.js loaded by the app proxy) but
      add-to-cart fails with "form data not found" because the
      variant form scaffolding isn't injected.
    {%- endcomment -%}

    {%- render 'longeva-meta-robots' -%}
    {%- render 'longeva-schema-website' -%}
    {%- render 'longeva-schema-article' -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Pharmacy/MedicalBusiness JSON-LD rendered sitewide. Service, hub
      and article schemas reference @id #pharmacy and need this node to
      resolve on the same page. Skipped on cart, checkout, password and
      account routes where commercial entity schema is not appropriate.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- unless request.page_type == 'cart' or request.page_type == 'password' or request.page_type contains 'customers' -%}
      {%- render 'longeva-schema-pharmacy' -%}
    {%- endunless -%}

    {% if request.design_mode %}
      {%- render 'theme-editor' -%}
    {% endif %}

    <script>
  if ('scrollRestoration' in history) {
    history.scrollRestoration = 'manual';
  }
</script>
    {{ content_for_header }}
  </head>

  <body class="page-width-{{ settings.page_width }} card-hover-effect-{{ settings.card_hover_effect }}">
    {% render 'skip-to-content-link', href: '#MainContent', text: 'accessibility.skip_to_text' %}
    <div id="header-group">
      {% sections 'header-group' %}
    </div>

    <script>
      // Inline header height and menu style calculations to prevent layout shift.
      // Wrapped in requestAnimationFrame so the synchronous offsetHeight reads
      // do not block first paint. The CSS variables this sets are consumed by
      // sticky offsets which carry sensible fallbacks (var(--header-group-height, 80px));
      // the values from this script refine the offset after first paint, not before.
      // Note: Updates in calculateHeaderGroupHeight(), updateTransparentHeaderOffset() and setHeaderMenuStyle() utilities.js should be kept in sync with this function
      window.requestAnimationFrame(function () {
      (function setHeaderHeighCustomProperties() {
        /*
         * Header calculation functions for maintaining CSS variables
         * Mimic calculateHeaderGroupHeight() in utilities.js
         */
        const header = document.querySelector('header-component');
        const headerGroup = document.querySelector('#header-group');
        const hasHeaderSection = headerGroup?.querySelector('.header-section');

        if (!header || !headerGroup) return;

        const headerTopRow = header.querySelector('.header__row--top');
        const headerHeight = header.offsetHeight;

        // Calculate the total height of the header group
        let headerGroupHeight = 0;
        const children = headerGroup.children;
        for (let i = 0; i < children.length; i++) {
          const element = children[i];
          if (element === header || !(element instanceof HTMLElement)) continue;
          headerGroupHeight += element.offsetHeight;
        }

        // Check for transparent header special case
        if (header.hasAttribute('transparent') && header.parentElement?.nextElementSibling) {
          headerGroupHeight += headerHeight;
        }

        // Set CSS variables
        document.body.style.setProperty('--header-height', `${headerHeight}px`);
        document.body.style.setProperty('--header-group-height', `${headerGroupHeight}px`);

        if (headerTopRow) {
          window.requestAnimationFrame(function () {
            document.body.style.setProperty('--top-row-height', `${headerTopRow.offsetHeight}px`);
          });
        }

        /**
         * Updates CSS custom properties for transparent header offset calculation
         * Mimic updateTransparentHeaderOffset() in utilities.js
         */

        if (!hasHeaderSection || !header?.hasAttribute('transparent')) {
          document.body.style.setProperty('--transparent-header-offset-boolean', '0');
          return;
        }

        const hasImmediateSection = hasHeaderSection.nextElementSibling?.classList.contains('shopify-section');

        const shouldApplyOffset = !hasImmediateSection ? '1' : '0';
        document.body.style.setProperty('--transparent-header-offset-boolean', shouldApplyOffset);
      })();

      (function setHeaderMenuStyle() {
        const headerComponent = document.querySelector('#header-component');
        if (headerComponent) {
          const isTouchDevice = 'ontouchstart' in window && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0;
          const overflowList = headerComponent?.querySelector('overflow-list');
          const hasReachedMinimum = overflowList && overflowList.hasAttribute('minimum-reached');
          headerComponent.dataset.menuStyle = isTouchDevice || hasReachedMinimum ? 'drawer' : 'menu';
        }
      })();
      });
    </script>

    <main
      id="MainContent"
      class="content-for-layout"
      role="main"
      data-page-transition-enabled="{{ settings.page_transition_enabled }}"
      data-product-transition="{{ settings.transition_to_main_product }}"
      data-template="{{ template }}"
    >
      {% render 'back-button' %}
      {{ content_for_layout }}
    </main>

    <footer>
      {% sections 'footer-group' %}
    </footer>

    {% render 'search-modal' %}

    {% if settings.quick_add or settings.mobile_quick_add %}
      {% render 'quick-add-modal' %}
    {% endif %}
  </body>
</html>
